WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:05.820
Horror and comedy are two genres that have
been linked since as far back as 1935's Bride

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:06.990
of Frankenstein.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:10.420
There's just something about laughter and
terror that works particularly well together.

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:14.320
Here are some of the best horror comedies
you may not have seen yet.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.940
​Life After Beth

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:21.150
Despite starring John C. Reilly and Aubrey
Plaza of Parks and Recreation, 2014's Life

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:23.180
After Beth never got all that much buzz.

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:27.580
As the title character, Plaza succumbs to
the lethal effects of a snakebite and comes

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:31.680
back as a zombie — but she doesn't know
she's a zombie, and neither does her boyfriend

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.070
Zach, played by Dane DeHaan.

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:38.609
But as Beth's condition gradually deteriorates
into the usual rotting, groaning, and people-eating,

00:00:38.609 --> 00:00:42.080
it becomes clear that being undead might be
a fate worse than...well, you know.

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:52.500
By that point in 
the story, other zombies are popping up as

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:56.639
well, and Zach has to accept that happily
ever after probably isn't in the cards.

00:00:56.639 --> 00:01:01.149
Life After Beth certainly isn't the only zombie
romantic comedy, but it's a particularly strong

00:01:01.149 --> 00:01:03.819
one, and definitely worth checking out.

00:01:03.819 --> 00:01:05.519
Gremlins 2: The New Batch

00:01:05.519 --> 00:01:08.070
Gremlins is a great horror comedy, but it's
hardly under-appreciated.

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:14.829
Its 1990 sequel, on the other hand, is often
unfairly dismissed as too silly, too over-the-top,

00:01:14.829 --> 00:01:16.509
and too outright ridiculous.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:19.700
But it's that ridiculousness that actually
makes it so much fun to watch.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:23.951
Whereas Gremlins takes place in a tiny town
straight out of the past, Gremlins 2: The

00:01:23.951 --> 00:01:28.899
New Batch unfolds in an absurdly high-tech
skyscraper and introduces a preposterous batch

00:01:28.899 --> 00:01:29.899
of new gremlins.

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:33.340
"Brainy Gremlin, Spider Gremlin, Bat Gremlin,
Lady Gremlin, Googly-Eyed Gremlin, Electricity

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:37.320
Gremlin, Hulk Hogan gonna be in the motherf---er,
I'ma throw in a Gremlin myself!

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:39.240
Vegetable Gremlin!"

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:43.460
If you watched the original but skipped The
New Batch, it's time to correct that mistake.

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:44.700
​Return of the Living Dead

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:50.210
1985's The Return of the Living Dead has long
been considered a cult classic, but it doesn't

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:54.850
come up in conversations nearly as often as
it did in the decade following its release.

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:58.950
This unofficial sequel to George Romero's
Night of the Living Dead pushes its zombie

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:03.439
narrative to new lengths while playing it
totally straight, despite being completely

00:02:03.439 --> 00:02:04.439
ridiculous.

00:02:04.439 --> 00:02:08.640
One of the zombies from the original incident
that supposedly inspired Romero's film has

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:13.300
been kept in the basement of a medical supply
company, and two employees accidentally release

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:16.060
it...along with a gas that spreads the zombie
virus.

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:20.280
It's campy and silly, but it's a lot of fun,
and it was the first movie to put brains on

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:21.840
the menu for zombies.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:25.400
"Brains."

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:27.920
Patchwork

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:33.420
This little-seen indie from 2015 is a totally
unique take on the Frankenstein idea.

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:37.629
It starts with three women who each have a
particularly bad night out at a club, and

00:02:37.629 --> 00:02:39.340
each end up pushing daisies.

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:43.980
But a mad scientist working for a shady company
stitches the three together to create a single

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:45.010
being.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:49.450
Almost inevitably, the patchwork woman takes
violent revenge on people who have wronged

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:54.099
all her component parts, which leads to a
massacre at a frat house, among other things.

00:02:54.099 --> 00:02:58.340
If you like your horror comedy a little more
on the darker side, this is definitely a movie

00:02:58.340 --> 00:02:59.780
to check out.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:00.780
Bubba Ho-Tep

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:06.159
Horror legend Don Coscarelli always had a
unique take on the genre, as any Phantasm

00:03:06.159 --> 00:03:07.159
fan knows.

00:03:07.159 --> 00:03:11.110
But his 2002 film Bubba Ho-Tep is truly unlike
anything else.

00:03:11.110 --> 00:03:15.129
The title character is a cowboy mummy who's
menacing an old folks' home where one of the

00:03:15.129 --> 00:03:18.430
residents is an aging Elvis Presley, played
by Bruce Campbell.

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:22.420
"I felt my pecker flutter once like a pigeon
having a heart attack.

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:25.730
Then it laid back down and remained limp and
still."

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:30.250
To stop this supernatural menace, Elvis will
have to team up with Jack, an elderly black

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:32.310
man who thinks he's John F. Kennedy.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:37.439
Bubba Ho-Tep is a surprisingly touching movie
about growing old and accepting your mortality,

00:03:37.439 --> 00:03:41.659
but it's also a movie where JFK and Elvis
fight a cowboy mummy, and that's every bit

00:03:41.659 --> 00:03:44.480
as amazing as it sounds.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:45.480
Slither

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:49.430
Eight years before he took the helm of Marvel's
Guardians of the Galaxy, writer/director James

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:53.600
Gunn made his feature debut with the 2006
horror comedy Slither.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:58.159
Drawing inspiration from a wide variety of
sci-fi horror films, it's set in a small town

00:03:58.159 --> 00:04:02.760
that's invaded by space slugs that take over
people's bodies and turn them into zombies.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:06.579
With a cast that includes Elizabeth Banks,
Nathan Fillion, and Michael Rooker, this is

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:12.470
a movie that never stops moving at full speed,
combining verbal comedy, action, and over-the-top

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:13.950
gross-out effects.

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:15.079
​The Stuff

00:04:15.079 --> 00:04:21.190
1985's The Stuff definitely has a unique horror
premise: what if a wildly popular new dessert

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:23.300
on the market was actually evil?

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:26.380
Nobody knows what the Stuff is, but everybody
wants to eat it.

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:30.320
Well, almost everyone — because young Jason
thinks it's gross and swears he once saw it

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:31.500
move on its own.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:35.790
When his family loses interest in everything
except eating more Stuff, Jason teams up with

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:39.510
a former FBI agent to investigate what it
is and where it comes from.

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:44.530
The Stuff turns out to be a mysterious substance,
mined from deep within the Earth, that causes

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:47.070
those who eat it to become mindless zombies.

00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:50.710
Now it's up to Jason and his partner to stop
it before it takes over the world.

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:55.900
The Stuff is very 1980s in both its aesthetics
and its satire of consumerism, but it's still

00:04:55.900 --> 00:05:00.500
a fun movie to watch when you're looking for
scares you can't take too seriously.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.840
The Raven

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:07.130
This Roger Corman movie from 1963 doesn't
have much in the way of a plot, but its cast

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:08.130
is pretty amazing.

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:12.920
Corman mainstay Vincent Price is joined by
fellow horror legends Peter Lorre and Boris

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:15.530
Karloff, along with future legend Jack Nicholson.

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:20.710
The movie starts with Edgar Allan Poe's poem,
as a retired magician named Dr. Craven mourns

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:24.740
his wife Lenore and finds his study invaded
by a talking raven — who turns out to be

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:28.190
a transformed sorcerer looking for help regaining
his human shape.

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:31.990
He also reveals that Lenore hasn't kicked
the bucket after all — she's at the castle

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:33.340
of the evil Scarabus.

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:37.350
Once the three are united on-screen, they
seem to pretty much give up on the script

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:39.120
in favor of just goofing off together.

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:43.340
But if you're a fan of vintage horror, watching
this trio do what they do best is a unique

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:44.800
delight.

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:46.410
What We Do in the Shadows

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:52.320
Jemaine Clement and Taika Waititi co-directed
and starred in 2014's What We Do in the Shadows,

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:57.150
which takes the mockumentary format and applies
it to vampires, to hilarious effect.

00:05:57.150 --> 00:06:01.100
The fictional documentary follows four New
Zealand housemates who happen to be immortal

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:02.100
vampires.

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:05.740
Each of them carries the values and habits
of the eras in which they were born, which

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:09.230
leads to real-life conflicts… like whose
turn it is to clean up the kitchen.

00:06:09.230 --> 00:06:12.940
"The point is Deacon is that you have not
done the dishes for five years."

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:13.940
"That's right.

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:18.130
It's unacceptable to have so many bloody dishes
all over this bench."

00:06:18.130 --> 00:06:22.160
What We Do in the Shadows might be the best
new horror comedy of the last five years,

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:26.530
and its buzz is bound to grow with the release
of the Waititi-directed Thor: Ragnarok.

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:30.130
If you haven't seen it, it's worth checking
out now, before people start asking you how

00:06:30.130 --> 00:06:31.910
you've possibly avoided this classic.

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:34.440
It's so good...it's scaaaaaary.

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:37.380
Thanks for watching!

00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:39.890
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:39.890 --> 00:06:42.210
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

